patrone-terminal (0.1.4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Escape clears the command being typed at a shell's prompt, as in
    Windows' terminals, in a root shell from sudo su too. Programs that use
    Escape, such as vim, less, htop and mc, still get it. Preferences has a
    switch for it, "Escape clears the command line", on by default; turn it
    off to keep Escape for a shell's vi mode or as a stand-in for Alt.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:00:00 -0500

patrone-terminal (0.1.3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * A see-through background, as in Kali's terminal: the desktop shows
    faintly behind the text, 15% by default, while the title bar and tabs
    stay solid. Preferences has a Background transparency slider, from 0%
    (solid) to 60%.

